# Run artifacts are noise; the holdout audit log is not. It is the record of
# every look taken at the held-out segment, and it only does its job — making
# a second look visible — if it survives across sessions, clones and analysts.
# A log any one researcher can reset by cloning fresh is a decorative control.
#
# This must stay `runs/*` and never `runs/`: a directory-level ignore stops git
# descending into it at all, which silently kills the negation below.
# `.gitattributes` gives the log a union merge so concurrent appends from two
# branches do not conflict on every merge.
runs/*
!runs/holdout_audit.jsonl

